<!--
    Key bindings, loaded by the client on its own and never listed in the TOCs.
    Each name is what the client saves a player's key against, so a renamed
    binding needs its keys moved over (ns.MigrateBuffKeys,
    ns.MigrateSpellbookBinding).

    Toggle Enhanced Spellbook (Features/Enhanced-Spellbook/Key-Bindings.lua) calls
    a global, since Bindings.xml can call nothing else. Buff Duty's Buff Key
    (Features/Buff-Duty/Buff-Duty-Keys.lua) clicks a hidden secure
    button, which picks the next buff on the list and casts it; a macro clicks
    the same button: /click GtGBuffKey.

    MIGRATION (remove after 2026-12-03): the hidden binding is the spellbook
    toggle's name before the GtG name, kept so a key still saved against it
    keeps working until login moves it over. The Buff Key's old name,
    CLICK TFTBBuffIndividual:LeftButton, is deliberately not declared: a
    Thanks for the Buff from before Buff Duty moved here still ships that
    binding, and declaring it twice warns on every login. A CLICK binding
    needs no declaration to keep a saved key, and the old button name stays
    an alias (Buff-Duty-Keys.lua), so the key still works until login moves it.
-->
<Bindings>
	<Binding name="GOODTOGO_TOGGLE_SPELLBOOK" header="GOODTOGO" category="ADDONS">
		GoodToGo_ToggleSpellbook()
	</Binding>
	<Binding name="CLICK GtGBuffKey:LeftButton" category="ADDONS" />
	<Binding name="MACROSPELLBOOK_TOGGLE" category="ADDONS" hidden="true">
		GoodToGo_ToggleSpellbook()
	</Binding>
</Bindings>
